592186511333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186510914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511333 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "29cd7cba-3362-549f-8e3e-97da0f1c1325" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186511270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511411 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b4cd93bf-3a8c-5f18-b352-8eff8b26fc90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d6df4b5-e301-58fd-845a-847c7a249d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511494 #edb/ref 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =4.$ Computing $A-4I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 6 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{13}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95728" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "524b5d0d-afb1-56e2-9f18-7dc1697e2495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511495 #edb/ref 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((3)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]+(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511615 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511615 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3dcce81f-cc42-5948-b429-8ba4a11557f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511615 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511622 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511622 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "55f4143a-4a93-5e8d-b696-93cfb4a2e6c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511622 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511632 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511632 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f7d44ce-dbe3-5404-92b7-3a9a5ceebe0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511632 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511668 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511668 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d68ef3a3-b3f5-5888-8b3c-31c4716078a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511668 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511679 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f8df9c63-69f3-5acb-8e84-5b34d208def1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511679 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511494 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
